# Packages the dependency graph says this distro needs, which it leaves out on
# purpose. Each one is here because the binary that pulls it in is never run.
#
# The graph works on whole packages: it reports 'grub needs freetype' because
# one program in grub links it. 'make check' works on files and is the finer
# instrument - see check.ignore, which lists the individual binaries this
# accepts as unresolved.

# grub-mkfont builds the boot menu font, which the grub package already ships
# built. Resolving it pulls freetype, then harfbuzz, then icu, graphite2 and
# the C++ runtime out of gcc - 207 MB for a program the image never runs.
10-make-freetype
10-make-harfbuzz
10-make-graphite2
10-make-libpng
9-make-icu
8.29-make-gcc
8.22-make-mpfr
8.23-make-mpc
